WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.350
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C one, Book two.

2
00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:08.955
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.255 --> 00:00:15.658
Unit twenty-seven: Adaptation Studies. Today you will show how two changes are linked with 'the more …, the more …'.

4
00:00:15.958 --> 00:00:18.784
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:23.291
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.232
Adaptation.

7
00:00:26.217 --> 00:00:30.062
Adaptation means a new version of a work in a different form.

8
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:33.056
The film adaptation won three awards.

9
00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:36.059
Your turn. Say: Adaptation.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:40.122
Adaptation.

11
00:00:40.883 --> 00:00:42.059
Source text.

12
00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:46.617
Source text means the original work an adaptation is based on.

13
00:00:47.217 --> 00:00:49.437
Few viewers had read the source text.

14
00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:53.178
Your turn. Say: Source text.

15
00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:57.278
Source text.

16
00:00:58.017 --> 00:00:58.693
Film.

17
00:00:59.683 --> 00:01:02.496
Film means a story told through moving pictures.

18
00:01:03.083 --> 00:01:05.478
The film shortens the novel's second half.

19
00:01:06.083 --> 00:01:08.678
Your turn. Say: Film.

20
00:01:11.533 --> 00:01:12.233
Film.

21
00:01:12.983 --> 00:01:13.961
Fidelity.

22
00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:17.576
Fidelity means faithfulness to the original.

23
00:01:18.183 --> 00:01:21.030
Critics debated the film's fidelity to the book.

24
00:01:21.617 --> 00:01:24.629
Your turn. Say: Fidelity.

25
00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:28.398
Fidelity.

26
00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:30.430
Interpretation.

27
00:01:31.417 --> 00:01:35.111
Interpretation means a particular way of understanding a work.

28
00:01:35.717 --> 00:01:38.192
The director offers a darker interpretation.

29
00:01:38.783 --> 00:01:41.459
Your turn. Say: Interpretation.

30
00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:45.673
Interpretation.

31
00:01:46.417 --> 00:01:47.325
Medium.

32
00:01:48.317 --> 00:01:51.918
Medium means a form of communication such as film, print or theatre.

33
00:01:52.517 --> 00:01:54.760
Each medium has its own strengths.

34
00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:57.909
Your turn. Say: Medium.

35
00:02:00.767 --> 00:02:01.768
Medium.

36
00:02:02.517 --> 00:02:03.529
Audience.

37
00:02:04.517 --> 00:02:06.876
Audience means the people a work reaches.

38
00:02:07.483 --> 00:02:10.342
The adaptation attracted a younger audience.

39
00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:13.556
Your turn. Say: Audience.

40
00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:17.366
Audience.

41
00:02:18.117 --> 00:02:19.199
Transformation.

42
00:02:20.183 --> 00:02:23.518
Transformation means a complete change in form or character.

43
00:02:24.117 --> 00:02:26.894
The transformation of the ending angered fans.

44
00:02:27.483 --> 00:02:30.287
Your turn. Say: Transformation.

45
00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:34.622
Transformation.

46
00:02:35.433 --> 00:02:39.049
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:39.883 --> 00:02:42.963
Visal, did you prefer the novel or the film version?

48
00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:53.030
The novel, but the film is interesting. The more faithful the film tried to be, the less creative it seemed in the first hour.

49
00:02:54.117 --> 00:02:55.013
And later?

50
00:02:56.117 --> 00:03:03.494
The director took more risks. The further the film moved from the source text, the more powerful its images became.

51
00:03:04.583 --> 00:03:06.386
So is fidelity overrated?

52
00:03:07.483 --> 00:03:17.395
Partly. A film is a different medium. The more an adaptation thinks visually, the better it can capture the spirit, if not the letter, of the book.

53
00:03:18.533 --> 00:03:19.964
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:20.817 --> 00:03:24.360
Grammar focus: Comparative structures (the more, the more).

55
00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:25.789
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:26.483 --> 00:03:30.062
The more faithful the film, the less creative it may be.

57
00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:34.737
The further the film moved from the book, the more powerful its images became.

58
00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:39.763
The more an adaptation thinks visually, the better it captures the spirit.

59
00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:53.540
The double comparative shows that two things change together. Keep the order: the + comparative + subject + verb. The verb 'be' can be omitted in short forms: 'The more faithful the film, the less creative (it is).'

60
00:03:54.283 --> 00:03:59.107
Be careful! Don't say: The more faithful the film, the less it creative.

61
00:04:01.067 --> 00:04:04.703
Say: The more faithful the film, the less creative it is.

62
00:04:05.003 --> 00:04:09.151
Keep the order: the less + adjective + subject + verb.

63
00:04:09.967 --> 00:04:12.515
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:14.661
Beyond Fidelity.

65
00:04:14.961 --> 00:04:20.954
Discussions of adaptation have long been dominated by a single question: is it faithful to the book?

66
00:04:21.967 --> 00:04:28.146
Adaptation scholars argue that this question is limited, since every medium tells stories in different ways.

67
00:04:29.133 --> 00:04:35.754
A novel can spend pages inside a character's mind, whereas a film must show thought through image and performance.

68
00:04:36.767 --> 00:04:42.621
The more seriously we take these differences, the less sense it makes to judge films only by their fidelity.

69
00:04:43.633 --> 00:04:49.882
Instead, critics increasingly evaluate adaptations as interpretations that enter into dialogue with their source.

70
00:04:50.967 --> 00:04:55.166
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:56.017 --> 00:04:58.016
The more you practise, blank you become.

72
00:04:58.316 --> 00:05:02.643
A, the more confident. B, more confident. C, the most confident.

73
00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.478
The answer is A: the more confident.

74
00:05:09.617 --> 00:05:11.361
Choose the correct sentence.

75
00:05:11.661 --> 00:05:21.224
A, The more faithful the film, the less creative it is.. B, More faithful the film, less creative it is.. C, The more faithful is the film, less it creative..

76
00:05:24.767 --> 00:05:28.659
The answer is A: The more faithful the film, the less creative it is..

77
00:05:29.817 --> 00:05:33.326
The original work that an adaptation is based on is the blank.

78
00:05:33.626 --> 00:05:37.709
A, medium. B, source text. C, transformation.

79
00:05:41.267 --> 00:05:43.742
The answer is B: source text.

80
00:05:44.883 --> 00:05:46.732
Which collocation is correct?

81
00:05:47.032 --> 00:05:51.893
A, remain faithful to. B, stay faithfully with. C, keep faithful at.

82
00:05:55.433 --> 00:05:58.141
The answer is A: remain faithful to.

83
00:05:59.283 --> 00:06:03.303
According to the reading, critics increasingly see adaptations as…

84
00:06:03.603 --> 00:06:09.068
A, copies. B, interpretations in dialogue with the source. C, failures.

85
00:06:12.633 --> 00:06:16.374
The answer is B: interpretations in dialogue with the source.

86
00:06:17.567 --> 00:06:20.881
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:21.717 --> 00:06:24.494
Should a film adaptation be faithful to the book?

88
00:06:41.283 --> 00:06:42.772
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:43.072 --> 00:07:21.700
In my opinion, a film adaptation should be faithful to the spirit of a book, but not necessarily to every detail. The more a director tries to include every scene, the slower and less cinematic the film often becomes. For example, many fantasy films cut minor characters, yet they still capture the book's central themes. Fans who love the original sometimes feel betrayed by such changes. Even so, I believe a good adaptation should be judged as a new work in its own medium.

90
00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.640
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:29.501
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and comparative structures (the more, the more).

92
00:07:29.801 --> 00:07:34.833
Today's value is innovation. Try new ideas boldly, and learn from every attempt.

93
00:07:35.133 --> 00:07:37.658
See you in Unit twenty-eight. Goodbye!

94
00:07:37.958 --> 00:07:40.692
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

